==Etymology==
Atomix's name is a portmanteau of the word "atomic" and "mix", referencing his manipulation of nuclear energy as well as his ability to bring about nuclear fusion.

==Trivia==
*Similar to [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]], [[Echo Echo]], and [[Ultimate Echo Echo]], Atomix gives names to his attacks and moves.
*Atomix is one of [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]]'s favorite aliens. In fact, Ken seemed to be most excited to turn into Atomix than any other alien when he got his [[Omnitrix (Ken's Replica)|Omnitrix]].<ref>''[[Ken 10]]''</ref>
*Atomix is the only alien to have been unlocked by accident in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' and was the only one overall to have been done so by [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]].
**Atomix is also one of three aliens to have been unlocked by Azmuth, the others being [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]] and [[Bullfrag]].
*Atomix is Ben's second most powerful alien, the overall most powerful being [[Alien X (Classic)|Alien X]].{{Refn|[[:File:Atomix is Ben's Second Most Powerful Alien.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Atomix cannot transmute matter.{{Refn|[[:File:Atomix Cannot Transmutate Matter.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Atomix's powers are largely unexplored.{{Refn|[[:File:Atomix's Powers Unexplored.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*Even though Atomix has a [[Galvan (Classic)|Galvan]] tech symbol on his chest, it does not necessarily mean that [[Atomix's Species|his species]] is related to the Galvan in any way, shape or form.{{Refn|[[:File:Atomix's Species Not Connected to Galvans.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*A hypothetical [[Ultimate Forms|Ultimate]] version of Atomix would be very dangerous, emitting so much radiation that not only must one stand at least 40 feet away from him, but he would also necessitate a [[Prypiatosian-B Containment Suit|containment suit]] similar to [[NRG]]'s.{{Refn|[[:File:Ultimate Atomix Concept.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Atomix was first mentioned in ''[[Ken 10]]''; at the time, there were never any plans to design him during the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' as characters without screen time would be an undesirable financial expense to the studio.{{Refn|[[:File:No Plans To Design Atomix and Toepick in OS.png]]|group = TNP}}
**Incorporating Atomix into '''Omniverse''' and giving him a physical form and powers was [[Derrick J. Wyatt]]'s idea.{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Thought of Atomix and Toepick.PNG]]|group = DJW}} He was first revealed in a sneak peek of Arc 4.
**Atomix was designed by Dou Hong,{{Refn|[[:File:Dou Hong Designed Atomix.png]]|group = DJW}} based on Derrick's sketches.{{Refn|[[:File:Atomix Concepts.png]]|group = ca}}{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Designed Atomix Sketches.png]]|group = TNP}} Had [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]] designed him when his name was first conceptualized, he would have likely looked different.{{Refn|[[:File:OS Atomix and Toepick Would Look Different.png]]|group = TNP}}
*The way Atomix charges his attacks is based on Goku's Kamehameha chant in the '''[[Wikipedia: Dragon Ball|Dragon Ball]]''' franchise.{{Refn|[[:File:Atomix Goku Reference.png]]|group = DJW}} Atomix's tendency to name and announce his attacks is a trope found in various action anime and manga.
**However, it sounds like the "Homina Homina Homina" exclamation of Ralph Kramden from '''[[Wikipedia:The Honeymooners|The Honeymooners]]'''.
*Atomix's voice is similar to those of Aquaman from '''[[Wikipedia:Batman: The Brave and the Bold|Batman: The Brave and the Bold]]''' and [[w:c:thrilling-adventure-hour:The Adventures of Captain Laserbeam|Captain LaserBeam]] from '''[[Wikipedia:Thrilling Adventure Hour|Thrilling Adventure Hour]]''', both of which are traditional superheroes voiced by [[John DiMaggio]].
*There were no plans for Atomix to appear in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]].{{Refn|[[:File:RB No Atomix in Season 5.png]]|group = DR}}

